WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.360
Let's first understand what dilute and

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.340
concentrated mean generally.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.160
the most important thing about these terms is that they are relative.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.280
What do I mean by relative?

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.620
Here are two beakers on the screen.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.860
One on the left, and one on the right.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.360
And both have 100 ml of some colorless solvent.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.260
Now in the beaker on the left, I add 20 ml of some red solute.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.260
And on the right, I add 50 ml of the same red solute.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.760
In this case, we say that the solution on the right is concentrated.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.240
And the one on the left is dilute.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.640
We are looking at these two relative to each other

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:50.040
And you can see, that the concentrated solution is more red in color

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.160
as compared to the dilute one.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.760
This is stronger we can say

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.080
Let me give you another example

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.940
We take two empty beakers again

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.900
both with 100ml of some solution

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:06.380
The first beaker has 20 ml of some solute

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.020
and 80 ml of solvent

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.000
and the second one has 25 ml of solute

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.840
and 75 ml of solvent

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:22.200
Which solution is more concentrated according to you?

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.360
yes it's the second one

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:29.100
because the proportion of solute is more, in the second beaker

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:32.165
now that you know what dilute and concentrated mean

00:01:32.165 --> 00:01:35.195
let's move on to understanding what

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.755
concentrated acids and bases are

00:01:38.145 --> 00:01:40.435
in cases of acids

00:01:40.435 --> 00:01:43.415
water is considered to be a solvent and the acid added

00:01:43.415 --> 00:01:46.335
to the water is the solute. So we have

00:01:46.335 --> 00:01:49.215
one beaker on the screen here with some water and we add

00:01:49.215 --> 00:01:50.585
acid to it

00:01:51.175 --> 00:01:53.945
as the amount of acid I'm adding to the beaker is

00:01:53.945 --> 00:01:55.285
increasing

00:01:55.735 --> 00:01:58.635
the solution is getting more and more concentrated

00:01:59.025 --> 00:02:01.935
now let me ask you an interesting question!

00:02:01.935 --> 00:02:04.915
When I'm mixing acid and water, should we

00:02:04.915 --> 00:02:08.285
add water to the acid, or should we add acid to the water?

00:02:08.645 --> 00:02:11.615
To know the answer, what we should know is that

00:02:11.615 --> 00:02:14.745
the process of dissolving an acid or base in water is

00:02:14.745 --> 00:02:17.555
highly exothermic, which means

00:02:17.555 --> 00:02:20.585
a lot of heat is generated

00:02:20.585 --> 00:02:23.745
Now if we add water to the acid, the heated generated may

00:02:23.745 --> 00:02:27.060
cause the mixture to splash out, which may cause severe burns

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.840
And the glass container which contains the solution

00:02:29.845 --> 00:02:32.965
may also crack due to excessive heating

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:36.315
You would probably argue that the same would happen

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.820
when acid is added to the water, right?

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.260
Not really, and let me explain why

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.580
When we add acid to the water, the reaction will still be exothermic

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:49.360
But the water is a very good absorber of heat

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.640
Yes, unlike the acid the water

00:02:51.645 --> 00:02:53.095
absorbs the heat

00:02:53.835 --> 00:02:56.805
And that is why adding acid to water is better than

00:02:56.985 --> 00:03:00.145
doing it the other way around. But remember,

00:03:00.155 --> 00:03:03.225
the acid must be added very slowly, drop by drop

00:03:03.225 --> 00:03:06.085
and we should constantly stir the solution

00:03:06.765 --> 00:03:09.895
because if we add a lot of acid directly to water

00:03:10.155 --> 00:03:13.145
the heat generated will be so large that even

00:03:13.145 --> 00:03:15.645
water will not be able to absorb the heat.

